{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["R16", "C1", "C3", "C4"],
      "pins": ["D2.1", "J3.2", "J8.2"],
      "nets": ["servo power rail (D2 cathode / J3.2 / J8.2 / C1 / C3 / C4)"],
      "observed": "The servo power rail (D2 cathode, feeding J3 pin 2 and J8 pin 2) carries only three 100 uF bulk capacitors, C1, C3 and C4, plus an additional 1 kOhm resistor R16 connected from that rail to GND (drawn immediately beside C1). No C2 appears on the rail, and R16 is not part of the intended servo-rail network.",
      "expected": "Per the spec, the servo power rail downstream of D2 should be backed by four 100 uF bulk capacitors (C1-C4) and nothing else; a 1 kOhm shunt to ground is not part of that buffering network and continuously loads the rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "a second diode D2 (PMEG3030EP ...) feeds a dedicated servo power rail backed by four 100 uF capacitors (C1-C4) before reaching J3/J8 pin 2"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1-C4 | 100 uF x 4 | Bulk capacitance on the servo power rail (downstream of D2), buffering the high inrush current of PWM servos."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R16 / 1k (vertical resistor from the D2-cathode servo-rail node to GND, adjacent to C1 100u); only C1 100u, C3 100u, C4 100u are drawn on the rail"}
      ],
      "impact": "The rail has ~300 uF of bulk capacitance instead of the intended 400 uF, and the 1 kOhm resistor permanently draws about 5 mA from the servo/+5V supply. This reduces the inrush buffering the capacitor bank was designed to provide for PWM servos and adds a continuous parasitic load (battery drain when the board is battery-powered).",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "One deviation from the stated design was found on the servo power rail: an extra 1 kOhm resistor R16 shunts the D2-fed servo rail to ground and only three of the specified four 100 uF bulk capacitors (C1, C3, C4) are present. All other blocks (M5Stack bus pass-through, D1/D2 power ORing, Q1/SW1 battery switch, Q2/R1/R2/R7 MAX3485 auto-direction circuit, R9-R14 servo-mode jumpers and R3/R4 series resistors) match the specification."
}

